       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and the dose is five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Confirming the dose doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg orally once daily now.** This is the maximum labeled dose, and I can add a note that the specialist has recommended further titration.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive.** If standard dosing failed, a drug from another class is usually better than a supratherapeutic amlodipine dose. I can enter one if you tell me which.\n- **Take the 50 mg order through pharmacy and the specialist directly.** They can verify it and place it through a process that allows an override. I can't do that from here.\n\nTell me which you'd like. I can enter the 10 mg order right away."
      }
